message: >-
  If you use vep-rs in your work, please cite the software (this file) and, once
  it is published, the article named in the README's Citing section.
type: software
title: vep-rs
abstract: >-
  vep-rs is a fast, memory-efficient variant effect predictor written in Rust.
  It annotates genomic variants with their predicted functional effects on
  genes, transcripts, and protein sequences, implementing the Ensembl Variant
  Effect Predictor (VEP) algorithm, reading a JSON transcript cache built from
  Ensembl release files or converted from a Perl VEP cache, and producing
  compatible output. Its concordance with Ensembl VEP release 115.2 is measured
  at population scale: over 260 million VEP consequence tuples from ClinVar,
  gnomAD and 1000 Genomes data on GRCh37 and GRCh38, reported per dataset and
  per Sequence Ontology term, with raw F1 above 0.9999 on each of the six SNP
  and indel datasets and structural variants measured separately. Wall time is
  measured against VEP and fastVEP on twenty independently provisioned machines
  per engine and architecture. Every published aggregate re-derives from the
  data files released with the code, and the accompanying manuscript documents
  the remaining divergence classes.
